---
import { appendices } from '../../data/appendices.mjs';
import { gates } from '../../data/protocol.mjs';
import { ROLES } from '../../data/roles.mjs';
import { adherence } from '../../data/ops.mjs';
const { role } = Astro.props;
const R = `/${role.id}`;
---

<div class="stack">
  <div class="note">
    <span class="lbl">A form is a capture surface for a gate, not a document beside the record</span>
    In the paper protocol these nine appendices are Word files someone prints, fills and files. Here each
    one is bound to the gate that produces it: closing Gate C writes Appendix B; recording an observation
    writes Appendix C; a fired stopping rule opens Appendix D with its clock already running. There is no
    step where a person transcribes the work they just did onto a form.
  </div>

  <div class="stats g4">
    <div class="stat"><div class="k">Forms in the suite</div><div class="v">{appendices.length}</div><div class="n">Appendices A–I</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="k">Bound to gates</div><div class="v">{appendices.filter((a) => a.boundTo.includes('Gate')).length}</div><div class="n">Written by protocol execution</div></div>
    <div class="stat is-warn"><div class="k">Filed</div><div class="v">{adherence.documentation.rate}%</div><div class="n">{adherence.documentation.formsFiled} of {adherence.documentation.formsRequired}</div></div>
    <div class="stat is-warn"><div class="k">Outstanding</div><div class="v">{adherence.documentation.outstanding.length}</div><div class="n">Named and assigned, not "missing"</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-head"><h3>Gate → form mapping</h3></div>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table class="tbl">
        <thead><tr><th>Gate</th><th>Name</th><th>Writes</th><th>Owner</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {gates.map((g) => {
            const owner = ROLES.find((r) => r.id === g.owner);
            const a = appendices.find((x) => x.id === g.appendix);
            return (
              <tr>
                <td><span class="chip mono" style="font-weight:700">{g.key}</span></td>
                <td><div class="t">{g.name}</div><div class="s mono tiny">{g.ref}</div></td>
                <td><a class="t" style="color:var(--navy-600)" href={`${R}/form/${g.appendix}/`}>Appendix {g.appendix} — {a ? a.title : ''}</a></td>
                <td class="s">{owner ? owner.role : g.owner}</td>
              </tr>
            );
          })}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid g2">
    {appendices.map((a) => {
      const owner = ROLES.find((r) => r.id === a.owner);
      return (
        <a class="card" href={`${R}/form/${a.id}/`} style="display:block">
          <div class="card-head">
            <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center">
              <span style="width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--navy-800);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:700;font-size:14px">{a.id}</span>
              <div>
                <h3>{a.title}</h3>
                <div class="tiny muted mono" style="margin-top:2px">{a.ref}</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            {a.optional ? <span class="chip held">Optional</span> : null}
          </div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="tiny" style="margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6">{a.purpose}</p>
            <div class="chip-row">
              <span class="chip">Owner: {owner ? owner.role : a.owner}</span>
              <span class="chip live">{a.boundTo}</span>
              {a.signatures.length ? <span class="chip warn">{a.signatures.length} signature{a.signatures.length > 1 ? 's' : ''}</span> : null}
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>
      );
    })}
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-head"><h3>Outstanding documentation</h3><span class="chip warn">{adherence.documentation.outstanding.length}</span></div>
    <div class="card-body flush">
      {adherence.documentation.outstanding.map((o) => (
        <div class="check open" style="grid-template-columns:22px 1fr auto">
          <span class="box" style="border-style:dashed"></span>
          <span><span class="cl">{o}</span></span>
          <span class="chip warn">Open</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="card-note">
      "Missing paperwork" is not a category here. Each open item names the patient, the form, the reason
      it is open and the person it is assigned to — because §7 requires 100 % of forms filed, and a
      number without a worklist behind it cannot be acted on.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
